    {
      "id": "b3ead333-d13d-4585-ad84-ae7d65a81123",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Is the relationship linear — or are there diminishing returns?\n\nBin matches by **possession differential** (home minus away) and look\nat the home win rate. If possession truly drives results, the curve\nshould keep climbing; a flattening top end would mean the last few\npercentage points of possession are worth little.",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "22cfbd66-7744-4e64-8c91-88f1481ec720",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "// home win% by possession differential (5-point bins)\nlet mut bins: Vec<(i64, usize, usize)> = Vec::new(); // (bin centre low, home wins, total)\nfor k in -7i64..=7 {\n    let lo = k as f64 * 5.0;\n    let hi = lo + 5.0;\n    let (mut hw, mut n) = (0usize, 0usize);\n    for r in &epl {\n        let d = r.hp - r.ap;\n        if d >= lo && d < hi {\n            n += 1;\n            if r.hg > r.ag { hw += 1; }\n        }\n    }\n    bins.push((k, hw, n));\n}\nlet d_rows: Vec<Vec<String>> = bins.iter().map(|(k, hw, n)| vec![\n    format!(\"{:+.0} to {:+.0}\", *k as f64 * 5.0, *k as f64 * 5.0 + 5.0),\n    n.to_string(),\n    format!(\"{:.1}%\", if *n > 0 { 100.0 * *hw as f64 / *n as f64 } else { 0.0 }),\n]).collect();\nmars_table(&[\"possession diff (home − away)\", \"matches\", \"home win%\"], &d_rows);\n",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 5,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "stat rows indexed: 374660\nmatches with valid possession (both teams): 111836\nEPL matches with possession: 8486 | all leagues: 111836\n"
